It does not apply to third-party materials or separately licensed project code.

The original functional code in scripts/ and .github/workflows/ is separately
available under LICENSES/MIT.txt. That MIT license does not extend to Media
Materials embedded in, read by, or produced by those scripts, including the
personal copy and PF mark, even when the output is generated automatically.
Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.

2. LIMITED MEDIA PERMISSION

Subject to these terms, Paul Fleury grants a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive, non-transferable permission to copy, display, and reproduce
the Media Materials for:

- editorial reporting, criticism, commentary, and biographical profiles
  concerning Paul Fleury or his work;
- factual author or contributor identification connected with such coverage;
- an event's identification of Paul Fleury as a participant, only after he
  has separately agreed to participate in that event.

An editorial publication may charge readers or carry advertising. That does
not, by itself, make its genuine editorial use ineligible.

You may share the relevant files with your publisher, designer, or production
provider solely to complete the permitted use on your behalf, provided they
follow the same restrictions. They receive no independent reuse rights.

3. CREDIT AND CONTEXT

Credit the portrait as "Paul Fleury / supplied portrait". Credit a graphic as
"Paul Fleury / mediakit". For online use, include a reasonably accessible link
to https://github.com/paulfxyz/mediakit or https://paulfleury.com. For print,
include paulfleury.com where practical. Do not imply that this credit identifies
the photographer or an independent certifier.

Keep quotations faithful and identify personal statements as Paul Fleury's
own account. Biographies may be excerpted, paraphrased, or translated for the
permitted purposes without materially changing their meaning or inventing
credentials, medical details, associations, or endorsements.

The permission does not require favourable coverage, approval of an article,
or prior review of independent journalism. Criticism is permitted.

4. PORTRAIT AND GRAPHIC MODIFICATIONS

You may convert file formats, compress files, proportionally reduce their size,
and make a conventional crop that preserves the subject and context. Supplied
circular masks and the 4:5 crop are permitted versions of the same photograph.

No portrait export may be enlarged beyond its supplied pixel dimensions.
The maximum supplied portrait dimension is 512 pixels. Do not use AI upscaling,
face enhancement, facial reconstruction, face or body alteration, synthetic
animation, or generative extensions under this permission.

Do not recolour or alter the portrait's appearance. Do not materially change
the PF marks, or use a graphic in a way that misrepresents a project, its
availability, or its relationship to Paul Fleury.

5. USES REQUIRING SEPARATE WRITTEN PERMISSION

This permission does not authorise:

- advertising, paid promotion, commercial endorsements, or suggestions of
  sponsorship or affiliation;
- merchandise, stock-photo distribution, resale of the Media Materials as
  standalone assets, or licensing them onward for unrelated uses;
- impersonation, fake accounts, deepfakes, synthetic likenesses or voices,
  or invented recordings of Paul Fleury;
- use of Media Materials in biometric identification datasets, face-recognition
  systems, or model training or fine-tuning datasets;
- reuse of another photograph, avatar, video, or recording merely because
  it depicts or is associated with Paul Fleury online;
- publication of the unpublished original or an unapproved higher-resolution
  derivative.

These restrictions state what this permission grants. They do not assert
control over an act for which no permission is required under applicable law.

